  "instructions": [
    "Add new objects at the end of the hashes array.",
    "Supported algorithms are SHA256 and SHA1.",
    "Use filenames when known so the scanner hashes that name anywhere on selected drives.",
    "Generic names such as index.js, main.js, package.json, settings.json, tasks.json, and bundle.js are not forced globally; keep Deep package-script hashing enabled for those files.",
    "Entries are loaded at startup and before every scan; no rebuild is required.",
    "Invalid entries are skipped and recorded only when the scanner is launched with --debug. Built-in hashes remain active.",
    "The final SHA1 entry is a harmless detection test for a file named testfile.js containing the documented test text."
